WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.157
Materialized views still need a clear grain.

00:00:03.157 --> 00:00:07.477
In this example, one row represents one diagnosis.

00:00:07.477 --> 00:00:11.182
The measures summarize admissions for that diagnosis.

00:00:11.182 --> 00:00:15.832
The refreshed-at value records when the stored result was produced.

00:00:15.832 --> 00:00:21.122
Consumers need both the grain and freshness information to interpret the data correctly.

00:00:21.122 --> 00:00:26.572
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:26.572 --> 00:00:33.647
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:33.647 --> 00:00:39.920
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
